<Prose title="Help" titleKey="nav.help">
  <p class="lead">ScriptureEarth helps you find the Bible in your language: to read, listen to, watch, or use on your phone.</p>

  <h2>Find a language</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Search.</strong> On the <a href="/">home page</a>, type a language name, another name for it, its three-letter code (such as <code>spa</code>), or a country. Matches appear as you type.</li>
    <li><strong>Browse.</strong> <a href="/browse/">Languages</a> lists every language. Use the Read, Listen, Watch, Apps and Buy buttons to show only languages that have that kind of resource.</li>
    <li><strong>By country.</strong> <a href="/countries/">Countries</a> lists countries by continent. Pick one to see its languages.</li>
    <li><strong>Map.</strong> The world map on the home page shades each country by how many of its languages have Scripture. Click a country to open it. On a phone, tap the map to zoom in, then pick a country from the list under the map.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>On a language page</h2>
  <p>Resources are grouped by what you can do with them:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Read</strong>: read online or download a PDF.</li>
    <li><strong>Listen</strong>: play or download audio recordings.</li>
    <li><strong>Watch</strong>: films and videos, such as the JESUS film.</li>
    <li><strong>Apps</strong>: Bible apps for Android and iPhone.</li>
    <li><strong>Buy</strong>: where to order printed Bibles and other materials.</li>
    <li><strong>Other</strong>: related websites, such as Global Recordings Network.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Many resources come from partner organizations and open on their websites. Each one shows its own copyright and license.</p>

  <h2>Change the site language</h2>
  <p>Use the language picker at the top of every page. The site remembers your choice on this device, and shows language and country names in that language where we have them.</p>

  <h2>Old links</h2>
  <p>Links and bookmarks to the old ScriptureEarth site still work: they take you to the matching page here.</p>

  <h2>Still stuck?</h2>
  <p><a href="/contact/">Contact us</a> and tell us what you were looking for.</p>
</Prose>
